2. MODULO OPERATOR %
it returns the remainder of a division.
(whatever is left over after dividing)
result = dividend % divisor
result = 10 % 3
result = 1
when the dividend is smaller than the divisor, the result is simply the dividend itself.
usually it is used for checking if a number is even or odd.
even number
number % 2 == 0
odd number
number % 2 == 1
3. ARITHMETIC SHORTCUTS
+=
-=
*=
/=
%=
example
instead of writing:
a = 5
a = a + 3   # a holds 8
we can simplify it by writing +=:
a = 5
a += 3   # a holds 8
the += operator adds the value 3 to a.
4. COMPARISON OPERATORS
==         Equal                   1 == 2 returns False
!=        Not Equal                1 != 2 returns True
>        Greater Than              1 > 2 returns False
<          Less Than               1 < 2 returns True
>=     Greater Than or Equal       1 >= 2 returns False
<=	    Less Than or Equal         1 <= 2 returns True

